s (e.g. a small hand-verified expected-verdict table per kind, or an existing upstream semantics tool if one exists at the pinned commit), so OS2-C2 can fail for semantic mismatch, not just parse success.\",\"relevance\":\"hardening\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"title\":\"No independent oracle evaluates requires-formula semantics for the differential claim\"}\n{\"concern_id\":\"ossie-plan-roundtrip-vs-refused-elements\",\"evidence\":[{\"artifact_path\":\".gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-interchange/notes/ossie-interchange-plan.md\",\"location\":\"Predicate 5, lines 52-53; OD6 ruling, line 448; §2.1 objectification row, line 205\",\"observation\":\"Predicate 5 requires that 'for a GND-exported document, import restores a model that gnd diff reports as equal to the source (round trip, OS3-C3)', while OD6 (o) rules default export is 'Exit 0 with the loss report' even when elements are refused, and §2.1 marks objectification as 'extension, or refused (OS0 measures)'. A refused element is by definition not in the document, so import cannot restore it and the unqualified round-trip equality cannot hold for any census model that produces a refused disposition.\"}],\"recommendation\":\"Scope OS3-C3 explicitly: either restrict round-trip equality to documents whose loss report contains no refused rows (with those models listed in the OS3 spec) or require refused elements to be reconstructible from a recorded reason code; state which in the OS3 spec so the predicate is falsifiable as written.\",\"relevance\":\"hardening\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"title\":\"Round-trip predicate is unqualified for exports that contain refused elements\"}\n{\"concern_id\":\"ossie-plan-od-range-inconsistency\",\"evidence\":[{\"artifact_path\":\".gnd-planning/milestones/ossie-interchange/notes/ossie-interchange-plan.md\",\"location\":\"Header, line 3; §1.4 sources table, line 174; §10 OD8 row, line 450\",\"observation\":\"The header states 'The owner ruled OD0–OD7 on 2026-11-10', but §1.4 cites 'rulings O